92186045417] [17592186097749 1061 461037 17592186045417] [17592186097749 1062 #uuid "91e627df-d8f4-581a-bf44-76bf1bb88674" 17592186045417] [17592186097749 1063 17592186097806 17592186045417] [17592186097806 1064 "Now, let's derive the rule\n![](images/77/77334bed6aafc3383552d90bcfc8da614d56493edce4e7ab89a2f28e01d3dbfa.svg)\n\nThe trick here is to write this in terms of ![](images/5b/5ba79af546498192229d0cdd5a4a922d1d015802402b8eec5910fe00f999820d.svg) \n\nFirst, note that since the natural logarithm is the inverse of the exponential function, we have\n![](images/09/091c69568c8472aacf8229a756a835e0edc26700677e4fa67de3d2f6ac0d96a2.svg)\n\nand by the power rule for logarithms, we can write this as\n\n![](images/c9/c9b146d550ef068823a4ee4b9f63eea89f46d6ceecedf0ad4baa6462f11d9127.svg)\n\nNow, the following result can be used (we'll prove it in the subsequent topics):\n\n![](images/ce/cedfc7ab127ac8b34cd72b21e8c3e527541e054721324d9d948d6df123cd61e0.svg)\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n![](images/58/5880fb665abda7f3cef4ad7425c99c43b16e84c448c7b9e22ff32f76e36df87c.svg)\n\nas required." 17592186045417] [17592186097806 1065 13257 17592186045417] [17592186097806 1066 #uuid "551a7005-80c0-5cee-b28e-f3b565aaf250" 17592186045417] [17592186097806 1067 "Justifying the Second Rule" 17592186045417] [17592186097813 1064 "The exponential function  $f(x) = e^x$ has the special property that its derivative is the function itself:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{ \\textrm{d} x}\\left( e^x \\right)= e^x\n$$\n\nSo, taking the derivative of an exponential function does nothing to the exponential function. The exponential function remains exactly the same. \n\nNote that the exponential function is the *only* function with this special property.\n\nWe'll justify this result at the end of the lesson. But for now, let's get some practice working with it." 17592186045417] [17592186097813 1065 2611 17592186045417] [17592186097813 1066 #uuid "a71b1a8d-93f4-5e48-ab3a-bd7220d50f18" 17592186045417] [17592186097813 1067 "Introduction" 17592186045417] [17592186097814 1064 "If we replace  the base $e$ of an exponential function by any other positive number $a$, then the derivative is as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{ \\textrm{d} x}\\left( a^x \\right)= a^x \\ln a\n$$\n\nWe just multiply the given exponential function by the natural logarithm of the base.\n\nNote that since $\\ln e =1$, our first formula is a particular case of this one!\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{ \\textrm{d} x}\\left( e^x \\right)= e^x \\ln e = e^x \\cdot 1 = e^x\n$$" 17592186045417] [17592186097814 1065 2612 17592186045417] [17592186097814 1066 #uuid "061a5c54-700a-5793-b266-cf156584544a" 17592186045417] [17592186097814 1067 "Differentiating an Exponential Function with a Base Other Than e" 17592186045417] [17592186097815 1064 "To derive the identity\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(e^x) = e^x,\n$$\n\nwe begin with the definition of the derivative:\n\nwhere $f(x) = e^x$.\n\nSubstituting the function $f(x)$ into the definition of $f'(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={lim}_{h\\to 0}\\frac{{e}^{x+h}-{e}^{x}}{h} \\\\  & ={lim}_{h\\to 0}\\frac{{e}^{x}\\cdot {e}^{h}-{e}^{x}}{h} \\\\  & ={lim}_{h\\to 0}\\frac{{e}^{x}\\cdot ({e}^{h}-1)}{h} \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\cdot {lim}_{h\\to 0}\\frac{{e}^{h}-1}{h}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, it can be shown that\n\n$$\n\\lim_{h \\to 0} \\frac{e^h - 1}{h} = 1,\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\nf'(x) = e^x \\cdot 1 = e^x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(e^x) = e^x.\n$$" 17592186045417] [17592186097815 1065 2613 17592186045417] [17592186097815 1066 #uuid "1b006e01-04f6-5f6b-b435-b0f89163d7a1" 17592186045417] [17592186097815 1067 "Justifying the Rule for the Derivative of the Exponential Function" 17592186045417] [17592186234683 1080 "{e}^{x}+2x+1" 17592186045417] [17592186234683 1082 17592186045498 17592186045417] [17592186234683 1083 #uuid "58606740-b081-5671-ab93-5b28309b7d77" 17592186045417] [17592186235226 1075 17592186234683 17592186045417] [17592186235226 1076 17592186045492 17592186045417] [17592186235226 1077 "field-1" 17592186045417] [17592186235226 1078 17592186234683 17592186045417] [17592186235226 1079 #uuid "d0bd4a86-aed0-5919-98b7-ad23d53bddbe" 17592186045417] [17592186250976 1080 "{6}^{x}ln⁡6-10{x}^{2}+6x" 17592186045417] [17592186250976 1082 17592186045498 17592186045417] [17592186250976 1083 #uuid "3232bdcf-d781-5e59-bb5b-56c10f0d7fa1" 17592186045417] [17592186251009 1080 "{6}^{x}-10{x}^{2}+6x-19" 17592186045417] [17592186251009 1082 17592186045498 17592186045417] [17592186251009 1083 #uuid "37865371-b061-54aa-9810-81e59d0b835b" 17592186045417] [17592186251060 1080 "{6}^{x}ln⁡6-10x+6" 17592186045417] [17592186251060 1082 17592186045498 17592186045417] [17592186251060 1083 #uuid "3d09661f-ce26-5e19-a8b8-2ae50263662e" 17592186045417] [17592186251775 1080 "{6}^{x}-10x+6" 17592186045417] [17592186251775 1082 17592186045498 17592186045417] [17592186251775 1083 #uuid "9007950f-ce55-5f0c-a1f6-d3963f0294f9" 17592186045417] [17592186252214 1080 "{6}^{x}ln⁡6-10{x}^{2}+6x-19" 17592186045417] [17592186252214 1082 17592186045498 17592186045417] [17592186252214 1083 #uuid "bbf32e0c-8341-5060-b67e-c44870ab4cd0" 17592186045417] [17592186253210 1075 17592186250976 17592186045417] [17592186253210 1075 17592186251009 17592186045417] [17592186253210 1075 17592186251060 17592186045417] [17592186253210 1075 17592186251775 17592186045417] [17592186253210 1075 17592186252214 17592186045417] [17592186253210 1076 17592186045493 17592186045417] [17592186253210 1077 "selection" 17592186045417] [17592186253210 1078 17592186251060 17592186045417] [17592186253210 1079 #uuid "e849ca6e-9bda-5244-a669-0f22826facaa" 17592186045417] [17592186253334 1068 17592186253210 17592186045417] [17592186253334 1069 "q-11735" 17592186045417] [17592186253334 1070 17592186045485 17592186045417] [17592186253334 1071 "Given that $f(x)={6}^{x}-5{x}^{2}+6x-19$, find ${f}^{′}(x).$" 17592186045417] [17592186253334 1072 #uuid "50678a5c-afcb-522f-98fb-80e9680afca6" 17592186045417] [17592186253334 1074 "Applying the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({6}^{x}-5{x}^{2}+6x-19) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({6}^{x})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5{x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6x)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(19) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({6}^{x})-5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+6\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(19) \\\\  & =ln⁡6\\cdot {6}^{x}-5(2x)+6(1)-0 \\\\  & ={6}^{x}ln⁡6-10x+6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 17592186045417] [17592186269346 1080 "e+4" 17592186045417] [17592186269346 1082 17592186045498 17592186045417] [17592186269346 1083 #uuid "0884ad38-9d14-5f8e-b665-d8b35b5af237" 17592186045417] [17592186269388 1080 "e+8" 17592186045417] [17592186269388 1082 17592186045498 17592186045417] [17592186269388 1083 #uuid "0db0ac08-c4ce-5d3f-845f-d38358413506" 17592186045417] [17592186269472 1080 "8e" 17592186045417] [17592186269472 1082 17592186045498 17592186045417] [17592186269472 1083 #uuid "1859eb59-5659-5101-b949-46d66d579831" 17592186045417] [17592186269501 1080 "2+6e" 17592186045417] [17592186269501 1082 17592186045498 17592186045417] [17592186269501 1083 #uuid "1c0e81a7-1d07-50d3-b00e-dd0c50955d37" 17592186045417] [17592186269640 1080 "2e" 17592186045417] [17592186269640 1082 17592186045498 17592186045417] [17592186269640 1083 #uuid "2934301c-7684-5c1f-b910-d7819431eba3" 17592186045417] [17592186269679 1080 "1+6e" 17592186045417] [17592186269679 1082 17592186045498 17592186045417] [17592186269679 1083 #uuid "2d71f9f8-72d8-5409-b4ca-0645cd6983b2" 17592186045417] [17592186270328 1080 "2e+8" 17592186045417] [17592186270328 1082 17592186045498 17592186045417] [17592186270328 1083 #uuid "7789397b-7630-5bd8-9c80-42e72f128cee" 17592186045417] [17592186270388 1080 "2e+4" 17592186045417] [17592186270388 1082 17592186045498 17592186045417] [17592186270388 1083 #uuid "81639c