5 17592186524817 17592186045417] [17592186524926 1076 17592186045493 17592186045417] [17592186524926 1077 "selection" 17592186045417] [17592186524926 1078 17592186524817 17592186045417] [17592186524926 1079 #uuid "cb8c7399-82f9-563a-b941-a6a1414975f7" 17592186045417] [17592186524955 1075 17592186524450 17592186045417] [17592186524955 1076 17592186045492 17592186045417] [17592186524955 1077 "field-1" 17592186045417] [17592186524955 1078 17592186524450 17592186045417] [17592186524955 1079 #uuid "ff484f27-c600-5f6e-a8a7-362f170f3f67" 17592186045417] [17592186524982 1068 17592186524862 17592186045417] [17592186524982 1069 "q-340053" 17592186045417] [17592186524982 1070 17592186045485 17592186045417] [17592186524982 1071 "Given that $f(x)=9{e}^{x}-11,$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" 17592186045417] [17592186524982 1072 #uuid "451b7f5e-73c7-5775-8944-779b29e93099" 17592186045417] [17592186524982 1074 "The derivative of ${e}^{x}$ is just ${e}^{x}$ itself. On the other hand, $-11$ is a constant, so its derivative is $0.$\n\nUsing the addition rule, then, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(9{e}^{x}-11) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(9{e}^{x})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-11) \\\\  & =9\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})+0 \\\\  & =9{e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 17592186045417] [17592186524984 1068 17592186524874 17592186045417] [17592186524984 1069 "q-140439" 17592186045417] [17592186524984 1070 17592186045487 17592186045417] [17592186524984 1071 "Given that $f(x)=4\\cdot {2}^{x}+{x}^{3}-{e}^{2}$,  find the slope of the tangent at $x=0.$" 17592186045417] [17592186524984 1072 #uuid "46572da3-e0a7-57d7-a2f6-062b0d2adadb" 17592186045417] [17592186524984 1074 "Applying the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4\\cdot {2}^{x}+{x}^{3}-{e}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4\\cdot {2}^{x})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-{e}^{2}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot {2}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3})+0 \\\\  & =4\\cdot {2}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+3{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=0$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=0} & =(4\\cdot {2}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+3{x}^{2}){|}_{x=0} \\\\  & =4\\cdot {2}^{0}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+3\\cdot {0}^{2} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 1\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡2+3\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 17592186045417] [17592186525017 1068 17592186524955 17592186045417] [17592186525017 1069 "q-304018" 17592186045417] [17592186525017 1070 17592186045485 17592186045417] [17592186525017 1071 "Given that $f(x)=4{e}^{x}+17$, the slope of the tangent line at $x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡3$ is{{field-1}}." 17592186045417] [17592186525017 1072 #uuid "9cb89f9e-c6cf-5b21-994c-7efe5115b691" 17592186045417] [17592186525017 1074 "The derivative of ${e}^{x}$ is just ${e}^{x}$ itself. On the other hand, $17$ is a constant, so its derivative is $0.$\n\nFirst, using the addition rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4{e}^{x}+17) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4{e}^{x})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(17) \\\\  & =4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})+0 \\\\  & =4{e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡3$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} & ={(4{e}^{x})\\,|}_{x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\  & =4{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 17592186045417] [17592186525040 1068 17592186524926 17592186045417] [17592186525040 1069 "q-71061" 17592186045417] [17592186525040 1070 17592186045485 17592186045417] [17592186525040 1071 "Given that $f(x)=4{e}^{x}-5{x}^{3}-4$, find ${f}^{′}(x).$" 17592186045417] [17592186525040 1072 #uuid "c8792aa5-0567-5ee4-a5c8-0188d2815575" 17592186045417] [17592186525040 1074 "Using the addition and the power rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4{e}^{x}-5{x}^{3}-4) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4{e}^{x})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5{x}^{3})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4) \\\\  & =4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})-5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4) \\\\  & =4{e}^{x}-5(3{x}^{2})-0 \\\\  & =4{e}^{x}-15{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 17592186045417] [17592186542624 1043 17592186543608 17592186045417] [17592186542624 1043 17592186543656 17592186045417] [17592186542624 1043 17592186543657 17592186045417] [17592186542624 1043 17592186543663 17592186045417] [17592186542624 1043 17592186543676 17592186045417] [17592186542624 1044 17592186045464 17592186045417] [17592186542624 1045 "Differentiating Exponential Functions" 17592186045417] [17592186542624 1046 17592186543657 17592186045417] [17592186542624 1048 17592186046647 17592186045417] [17592186542624 1049 17592186048749 17592186045417] [17592186542624 1053 #uuid "943d4724-4157-55d1-a2b7-c6967297f552" 17592186045417] [17592186542713 1080 "{f}^{′}(x)=5{e}^{x}+4{x}^{2}-3" 17592186045417] [17592186542713 1082 17592186045498 17592186045417] [17592186542713 1083 #uuid "1c78d12d-e0a1-56ab-9f9b-0b5ab3109e1b" 17592186045417] [17592186542728 1080 "{f}^{′}(x)={e}^{x}+4x" 17592186045417] [17592186542728 1082 17592186045498 17592186045417] [17592186542728 1083 #uuid "207cc40d-fc6f-5da2-b43d-321cce4f0d3b" 17592186045417] [17592186542780 1080 "5\\ln 7" 17592186045417] [17592186542780 1082 17592186045498 17592186045417] [17592186542780 1083 #uuid "3481b85e-58eb-5313-8a75-21e00c14674a" 17592186045417] [17592186542874 1080 "-6\\ln 2" 17592186045417] [17592186542874 1082 17592186045498 17592186045417] [17592186542874 1083 #uuid "5669689b-d4c2-598a-9b8e-4640a33a9697" 17592186045417] [17592186542988 1080 "12\\ln 4-2e" 17592186045417] [17592186542988 1082 17592186045498 17592186045417] [1759218654